WEBVTT

STYLE
::cue(c.color9CD5FF) { color: #9CD5FF; }

1
00:00:01.000 --> 00:00:07.000 line:5% align:center
<b><c.color9CD5FF>One Pace Addon</c></b>

2
00:01:30.110 --> 00:01:35.120
<b>Inside Pangaea Castle
The Holy Land, Mary Geoise</b>

3
00:01:31.690 --> 00:01:33.650
[thudding]

4
00:01:33.650 --> 00:01:35.780
[SOLDIER A grunts]

5
00:01:35.780 --> 00:01:38.030
[SOLDIER B growls]

6
00:01:38.080 --> 00:01:41.710
<b>The Attempted Murder
of a Celestial Dragon</b>

7
00:01:40.000 --> 00:01:43.630
[SOLDIER B] Give those
back! You'll pay for this!

8
00:01:54.780 --> 00:01:56.780
[SOLDIER D yells]

9
00:02:01.940 --> 00:02:05.030
[SOLDIER F yells]

10
00:02:23.190 --> 00:02:24.440
[gasps]

11
00:02:24.790 --> 00:02:25.960
[BONNEY] You're Sabo, right?

12
00:02:26.160 --> 00:02:30.590
Huh? Wait a sec.
You're Jewelry Bonney!

13
00:02:30.780 --> 00:02:33.410
If you know who I am,
then that saves us some time.

14
00:02:33.490 --> 00:02:35.360
I think we have the same goal.

15
00:02:37.380 --> 00:02:38.970
[SOLDIER G] Intruders
in the guardroom!

16
00:02:40.310 --> 00:02:41.690
They've stolen the keys
to the slaves' collars!

17
00:02:41.770 --> 00:02:43.070
Kill them on sight!

18
00:02:45.490 --> 00:02:47.890
[SABO] I knew Kuma had
a daughter, but that's all.

19
00:02:47.940 --> 00:02:49.120
[BONNEY] We've
never met before,

20
00:02:49.120 --> 00:02:51.810
but I've been keeping up
with your group for a while.

21
00:02:51.810 --> 00:02:54.520
Point is, I know you
guys are my allies,

22
00:02:54.520 --> 00:02:56.380
and I trust you
to save my dad!

23
00:02:56.380 --> 00:02:59.330
We will. That's what
we're here for.

24
00:03:03.560 --> 00:03:05.650
– Karasu!
– [KARASU] I'm here.

25
00:03:05.650 --> 00:03:09.280
I found the keys! Take them
and tell the other captains.

26
00:03:09.370 --> 00:03:11.920
Once you rescue Kuma
and unlock the slave collars,

27
00:03:11.920 --> 00:03:13.610
go straight back to HQ.

28
00:03:14.350 --> 00:03:16.120
Your mission will be complete!

29
00:03:17.620 --> 00:03:20.280
We don't have much
time. Go! And hurry!

30
00:03:20.340 --> 00:03:21.730
[KARASU] What
about you, Sabo?

31
00:03:21.730 --> 00:03:22.620
[SABO] I'll be all right.

32
00:03:22.720 --> 00:03:24.440
I'll follow once I
finish my business!

33
00:03:24.540 --> 00:03:27.080
[KARASU] Got it. Be careful!

34
00:03:32.220 --> 00:03:34.850
I assume you'll be leaving
soon. What's next?

35
00:03:34.870 --> 00:03:36.790
I'll be going straight
to Egghead.

36
00:03:36.870 --> 00:03:37.850
All by yourself?

37
00:03:38.220 --> 00:03:39.020
Uh-huh.

38
00:03:39.500 --> 00:03:42.780
Y'sure that's smart? It's
World Government territory.

39
00:03:43.050 --> 00:03:44.210
It doesn't matter!

40
00:03:44.290 --> 00:03:46.780
I need Vegapunk
to restore my dad's mind!

41
00:03:47.300 --> 00:03:49.510
That's the whole
reason I went to sea!

42
00:03:49.510 --> 00:03:53.600
Hold on, do you really think he
can get Kuma back to normal?

43
00:03:53.610 --> 00:03:55.770
[BONNEY] Well,
I'm not leaving until he does it.

44
00:03:55.890 --> 00:03:59.060
So he'd better fix him or else!

45
00:04:00.320 --> 00:04:01.520
[SOLDIER H] There they are!

46
00:04:01.520 --> 00:04:04.180
This way! Hurry!

47
00:04:13.430 --> 00:04:14.440
[SOLDIER K] Where are they?

48
00:04:14.520 --> 00:04:15.160
Dammit.

49
00:04:15.240 --> 00:04:16.130
[SOLDIER I] They're gone!

50
00:04:17.390 --> 00:04:18.470
[SOLDIER H] How strange.

51
00:04:19.130 --> 00:04:21.120
I could've sworn
I saw someone.

52
00:04:21.120 --> 00:04:23.880
Thanks. Nice timing.

53
00:04:24.430 --> 00:04:26.310
[SOLDIER J] Why do they
insist on making things

54
00:04:26.310 --> 00:04:27.940
so difficult for us?

55
00:04:27.940 --> 00:04:30.230
There simply aren't enough
guards in this tower

56
00:04:30.230 --> 00:04:32.690
to patrol a space
as large as this.

57
00:04:32.710 --> 00:04:35.170
[SOLDIER H] What?
Surely you must've heard.

58
00:04:35.350 --> 00:04:38.250
We're short on manpower
because of "you know what."

59
00:04:38.420 --> 00:04:39.270
[SOLDIER J] Pardon?

60
00:04:39.270 --> 00:04:40.390
[gasps]

61
00:04:40.480 --> 00:04:41.990
[SOLDIER H] Apparently,
they saw it.

62
00:04:42.070 --> 00:04:43.130
[SOLDIER J] Saw what?

63
00:04:43.210 --> 00:04:44.550
[SOLDIER H]
The Lost Chamber.

64
00:04:44.630 --> 00:04:46.000
[SOLDIER K] Keep
your voice down, you fool!

65
00:04:46.080 --> 00:04:47.570
Don't even joke about that!

66
00:04:51.500 --> 00:04:52.400
Thanks, Sabo.

67
00:04:52.480 --> 00:04:54.480
Well, Egghead is
in the New World,

68
00:04:54.860 --> 00:04:57.380
so it looks like we're headed
in opposite directions.

69
00:04:57.460 --> 00:04:58.670
[SABO] Just be careful.

70
00:04:58.670 --> 00:04:59.920
Okay.

71
00:04:59.940 --> 00:05:01.490
I'll keep you in my thoughts.

72
00:05:01.510 --> 00:05:05.030
Huh? Thanks,
but this is weird.

73
00:05:05.030 --> 00:05:06.050
[gasps]

74
00:05:06.100 --> 00:05:08.020
You're not a pirate like me.

75
00:05:08.210 --> 00:05:12.210
Dunno how I feel about
a Revolutionary treating me nice.

76
00:05:13.710 --> 00:05:15.860
We both wanna
save Kuma, right?

77
00:05:15.860 --> 00:05:16.920
Get him back safe.

78
00:05:20.270 --> 00:05:24.930
[PETER] What do you wish to ask,
Cobra, King of Alabasta?

79
00:05:25.380 --> 00:05:26.390
Speak up.

80
00:05:28.960 --> 00:05:32.760
Well, I suppose I
should start at the beginning.

81
00:05:32.760 --> 00:05:35.240
It is said that roughly
800 years ago,

82
00:05:35.240 --> 00:05:37.780
there were 20 monarchs
who came together

83
00:05:38.290 --> 00:05:40.660
to form the World
Government as we know it.

84
00:05:41.160 --> 00:05:43.130
After creating
this new regime,

85
00:05:43.130 --> 00:05:46.690
they relocated
their families to Mary Geoise.

86
00:05:46.690 --> 00:05:50.400
Those families became known
as the Celestial Dragons,

87
00:05:50.480 --> 00:05:53.510
and they have reigned
for eight centuries.

88
00:05:53.750 --> 00:05:55.700
But there was no
supreme ruler.

89
00:05:55.940 --> 00:05:59.280
They all shared
their power equally.

90
00:05:59.530 --> 00:06:02.570
The Empty Throne is a monument
to that commitment.

91
00:06:03.100 --> 00:06:07.030
It symbolizes their promise
to never allow a dictator to reign.

92
00:06:07.050 --> 00:06:10.010
The 20 monarchs placed
their weapons at its feet,

93
00:06:10.010 --> 00:06:13.100
vowing that none
would sit upon it.

94
00:06:13.100 --> 00:06:15.100
Meanwhile,
in their homelands,

95
00:06:15.290 --> 00:06:17.750
new royal families
were selected.

96
00:06:17.960 --> 00:06:20.840
And those families have
been in power ever since.

97
00:06:21.050 --> 00:06:22.500
Therefore,
their names all differ

98
00:06:22.500 --> 00:06:24.570
from those
of the First Twenty.

99
00:06:24.680 --> 00:06:28.310
A new line of succession
was born in each nation.

100
00:06:28.420 --> 00:06:30.870
And yet Alabasta is different.

101
00:06:31.190 --> 00:06:33.690
Queen Lili of
the Nefertari Family

102
00:06:33.690 --> 00:06:36.950
was named one of the First
Twenty monarchs at the time.

103
00:06:37.040 --> 00:06:39.270
But she did not become
a Celestial Dragon.

104
00:06:39.470 --> 00:06:41.550
She returned to Alabasta.

105
00:06:42.170 --> 00:06:45.820
And we, the Nefertari Family,
still reign there to this day.

106
00:06:46.250 --> 00:06:47.830
I assume that is the reason

107
00:06:47.970 --> 00:06:52.190
there are only 19 weapons
surrounding the throne.

108
00:06:52.190 --> 00:06:56.480
What you've said is correct,
but what is your point?

109
00:06:56.480 --> 00:06:58.680
[COBRA] Well, I've been
perusing some old books

110
00:06:58.680 --> 00:07:01.180
we have in my country.

111
00:07:01.180 --> 00:07:04.140
Of course, none of those texts
predate the Void Century,

112
00:07:04.140 --> 00:07:06.280
so we cannot
know the full truth,

113
00:07:06.680 --> 00:07:08.800
but I still noticed
something odd.

114
00:07:09.200 --> 00:07:14.210
Lili is missing. Her name
is nowhere to be found.

115
00:07:16.850 --> 00:07:20.610
It would seem she never made it
back to the Kingdom of Alabasta.

116
00:07:21.470 --> 00:07:24.670
Her younger brother ruled
the country in her stead.

117
00:07:24.760 --> 00:07:27.110
Nothing else about
her fate was written.

118
00:07:27.730 --> 00:07:30.250
Could you tell me what
you know about that?

119
00:07:31.190 --> 00:07:36.370
Is that all you wish to ask?
About an 800-year-old story?

120
00:07:36.660 --> 00:07:39.950
As you said, the monarch
of the Nefertari Family

121
00:07:39.950 --> 00:07:43.030
did not choose to stay
like the others.

122
00:07:43.260 --> 00:07:46.470
But the belief was that she
returned to her country.

123
00:07:46.860 --> 00:07:49.830
No one knows why she left,
or where she ended up.

124
00:07:50.610 --> 00:07:52.790
Those details have
been lost to time.

125
00:07:54.360 --> 00:07:56.770
That is all we know I'm afraid.

126
00:07:58.880 --> 00:08:00.810
[COBRA] Then
what is the "D."?

127
00:08:02.220 --> 00:08:04.630
And why would you ask that?

128
00:08:04.680 --> 00:08:06.570
It's quite brief,
but there is a letter

129
00:08:06.570 --> 00:08:09.600
that Queen Lili wrote
800 years ago.

130
00:08:10.080 --> 00:08:13.790
Our family has passed it
down for generations now.

131
00:08:17.520 --> 00:08:20.520
<b>Pangaea Castle</b>

132
00:08:17.730 --> 00:08:19.480
[SHIRAHOSHI sceams]

133
00:08:26.000 --> 00:08:26.800
Please!

134
00:08:27.030 --> 00:08:28.650
You're hurting me!

135
00:08:28.650 --> 00:08:32.200
This isn't right!
Somebody stop him!

136
00:08:35.200 --> 00:08:37.620
It was hard work,
but I finally did it!

137
00:08:37.700 --> 00:08:39.640
I never gave up on my dream

138
00:08:39.720 --> 00:08:42.920
and now the giant
mermaid belongs to me!

139
00:08:42.970 --> 00:08:45.890
Good lad! She's all
yours! A fine catch!

140
00:08:45.910 --> 00:08:48.490
Please, someone help!
He's going to take me away!

141
00:08:48.490 --> 00:08:52.250
This is a nightmare! Oh,
my poor, sweet Shirahoshi!

142
00:08:52.260 --> 00:08:55.500
Ooh! I wonder what
I should feed her!

143
00:08:55.500 --> 00:08:56.900
I can't wait
for her to pick me up

144
00:08:56.900 --> 00:08:58.330
with her big, beautiful hands,

145
00:08:58.330 --> 00:09:01.240
and carry me
around town all day!

146
00:09:01.580 --> 00:09:04.270
Look at my new
pet, Shirahoshi!

147
00:09:04.350 --> 00:09:06.930
Now, stop looking
and get out of my way!

148
00:09:07.060 --> 00:09:08.300
[BOTH laugh]

149
00:09:08.300 --> 00:09:12.610
[CHARLOS]
Everyone loves me!

150
00:09:12.610 --> 00:09:12.620
[chuckles]

151
00:09:12.690 --> 00:09:16.120
And if you don't obey me,
I'll be sure to give you hell!

152
00:09:16.200 --> 00:09:16.950
I refuse!

153
00:09:17.590 --> 00:09:18.500
[grunts]

154
00:09:19.020 --> 00:09:20.170
Why won't anyone help?

155
00:09:20.260 --> 00:09:24.800
Why are you just watching?
Please, save me!

156
00:09:24.990 --> 00:09:25.820
Why now?

157
00:09:26.160 --> 00:09:29.340
My father and all our guards
are in the Council Tower.

158
00:09:29.340 --> 00:09:32.580
He doesn't own me!
This isn't right!

159
00:09:34.060 --> 00:09:36.000
It seems there's
only one option.

160
00:09:37.410 --> 00:09:40.180
[SHIRAHOSHI]
You'll help me?

161
00:09:40.260 --> 00:09:41.660
Run away, hurry!

162
00:09:42.520 --> 00:09:43.370
Oh, no.

163
00:09:43.420 --> 00:09:45.310
[CHARLOS] You! Mermaid!

164
00:09:45.450 --> 00:09:47.510
Are you being
rebellious already?

165
00:09:47.620 --> 00:09:49.180
I should have you flensed!

166
00:09:49.420 --> 00:09:52.190
Honestly, it's rude
of her to expect us to bail her out!

167
00:09:52.280 --> 00:09:53.660
She turned us down!

168
00:09:53.740 --> 00:09:56.210
We can turn down saving
her from slavery, right?

169
00:09:56.210 --> 00:09:59.180
That's right! I won't put
my neck on the line for her!

170
00:09:59.180 --> 00:10:00.110
Make way!

171
00:10:00.220 --> 00:10:03.580
You pathetic, filthy cowards
are as spineless as a jellyfish!

172
00:10:03.580 --> 00:10:04.610
[ALL scream]

173
00:10:04.610 --> 00:10:05.940
[ROYAL SON A] The princes!

174
00:10:05.940 --> 00:10:07.870
[ROYALS yelp]

175
00:10:07.970 --> 00:10:11.300
You can't fight! They'll
destroy your whole country!

176
00:10:11.390 --> 00:10:13.480
Huh?

177
00:10:13.480 --> 00:10:15.860
Sister, forgive us
for letting this happen!

178
00:10:16.170 --> 00:10:17.580
I'm so glad you're here!

179
00:10:17.670 --> 00:10:19.160
I just wish we'd come sooner!

180
00:10:19.290 --> 00:10:23.250
But you're safe now!
We'll set you free right away!

181
00:10:24.830 --> 00:10:25.910
Let's return home!

182
00:10:25.990 --> 00:10:28.560
We'll never come
to this cursed place again!

183
00:10:29.060 --> 00:10:30.280
Thank you, Fukaboshi.

184
00:10:30.370 --> 00:10:31.570
Oh, you're going home?

185
00:10:31.650 --> 00:10:33.560
That sounds like
a splendid idea to me.

186
00:10:33.650 --> 00:10:36.770
The mermaid stays as my pet,
and you get out of my hair.

187
00:10:36.770 --> 00:10:38.390
I don't want any fishmen.

188
00:10:38.430 --> 00:10:41.740
You bastard! Give her back!

189
00:10:42.080 --> 00:10:44.150
How dare you
treat her that way!

190
00:10:44.150 --> 00:10:45.440
[yells]

191
00:10:45.690 --> 00:10:47.990
You'll pay for this!

192
00:10:47.990 --> 00:10:50.150
[ALL yell]

193
00:10:51.270 --> 00:10:55.410
Kill them, Kuma.
My Invincible Slave!

194
00:10:56.470 --> 00:10:57.550
[chuckles]

195
00:10:57.550 --> 00:10:59.810
[ALL yell]

196
00:11:00.520 --> 00:11:03.240
Don't kill them! Please!

197
00:11:03.240 --> 00:11:04.790
[REBECCA] Shirahoshi!

198
00:11:04.790 --> 00:11:05.750
[SHIRAHOSHI] Rebecca!

199
00:11:06.550 --> 00:11:07.930
[REBECCA] We'll get
those chains off of you!

200
00:11:07.930 --> 00:11:10.780
Rebecca! It's
that creep again!

201
00:11:10.780 --> 00:11:13.890
I don't care who he is!
We'll stop him!

202
00:11:15.240 --> 00:11:16.870
Just checking, Mjosgard,

203
00:11:17.010 --> 00:11:19.080
but I can kick his ass
this time, right?

204
00:11:19.080 --> 00:11:22.750
Of course! I'll take full
responsibility for it!

205
00:11:24.550 --> 00:11:26.010
[FUKABOSHI] A pity
that a former Warlord

206
00:11:26.010 --> 00:11:28.890
has been reduced to this,
but I won't relent!

207
00:11:28.890 --> 00:11:32.750
Forward! Let's go!
Ryuboshi! Mamboshi!

208
00:11:32.750 --> 00:11:33.640
[RYUBOSHI, MANBOSHI]
Ready!

209
00:11:33.640 --> 00:11:36.030
Just kill them,
Kuma! It'll be fine!

210
00:11:36.030 --> 00:11:37.410
Even if they are royalty,

211
00:11:37.550 --> 00:11:40.240
there's no problem a little
money can't solve!

212
00:11:40.240 --> 00:11:41.940
They are just fish.

213
00:11:42.020 --> 00:11:43.720
How dare you!

214
00:11:44.570 --> 00:11:45.670
Please, calm down!

215
00:11:45.750 --> 00:11:47.940
You mustn't forget
you are royalty!

216
00:11:48.020 --> 00:11:49.230
Don't stop me!

217
00:11:49.310 --> 00:11:50.860
[MJOSGARD] Leave
it to them instead!

218
00:11:51.060 --> 00:11:52.200
[BOTH growl]

219
00:11:52.200 --> 00:11:55.440
Our sister is in trouble!
I can't just watch!

220
00:11:55.500 --> 00:11:58.100
Why do they have a right
to step up when we don't?

221
00:11:58.170 --> 00:12:01.550
Because they are pirates!
Think of your country!

222
00:12:01.630 --> 00:12:03.080
You could start a war!

223
00:12:03.090 --> 00:12:05.660
[growls] Damn
you, Mjosgard!

224
00:12:05.670 --> 00:12:07.130
Don't you dare
think I've forgotten

225
00:12:07.130 --> 00:12:09.260
the insult you dealt to me!

226
00:12:09.260 --> 00:12:13.930
Kuma! Kill Mjosgard
this instant!

227
00:12:15.520 --> 00:12:17.020
Huh?

228
00:12:20.270 --> 00:12:22.270
Tontatta Combat!

229
00:12:22.270 --> 00:12:25.110
Hasshoken Technique:
Drill Dragon!

230
00:12:25.110 --> 00:12:27.070
Sir Leo! Sir Sai!

231
00:12:27.250 --> 00:12:28.060
Don't do it!

232
00:12:28.280 --> 00:12:31.270
They'll put you to death!

233
00:12:30.400 --> 00:12:31.900
Tail Hammer!

234
00:12:31.270 --> 00:12:38.810
[yells]

235
00:12:32.040 --> 00:12:34.670
And a nail!

236
00:12:40.500 --> 00:12:42.530
Charlos!

237
00:12:43.920 --> 00:12:45.780
They killed him!

238
00:12:45.780 --> 00:12:50.010
Oh, the inhumanity!
This is murder!

239
00:12:50.100 --> 00:12:52.660
[NOBLE F] The murder
of a Celestial Dragon!

240
00:12:53.950 --> 00:12:56.760
Someone call
the admirals, now!

241
00:13:09.100 --> 00:13:13.060
Stop it, Kuma!
Please, don't do this!

242
00:13:13.060 --> 00:13:16.600
We came here to set
you free! Okay?

243
00:13:16.650 --> 00:13:19.530
You don't have to follow
their orders anymore!

244
00:13:19.550 --> 00:13:23.430
We can help you!
Let's go home together!

245
00:13:23.430 --> 00:13:24.890
[NOBLE G yells]

246
00:13:25.200 --> 00:13:26.790
What is a Giant doing here?

247
00:13:27.520 --> 00:13:29.480
– [KARASU] Morley!
– Karasu!

248
00:13:29.510 --> 00:13:31.970
[KARASU] I got the keys
from Sabo! Come on!

249
00:13:31.980 --> 00:13:32.930
[SOLDIER L] What is that?

250
00:13:33.010 --> 00:13:33.970
[SOLDIER M] An intruder?

251
00:13:34.050 --> 00:13:35.080
[SOLDIER N] That's Morley!

252
00:13:35.160 --> 00:13:37.450
A captain of
the Revolutionary Army!

253
00:13:37.560 --> 00:13:40.350
Going down! See ya!

254
00:13:43.770 --> 00:13:47.400
Oh, my son! What have
they done to you?

255
00:13:54.530 --> 00:13:56.290
[gasps]

256
00:14:01.590 --> 00:14:05.950
Great Imu! King
Cobra is still here!

257
00:14:05.950 --> 00:14:08.470
[COBRA] Did he say Imu?

258
00:14:22.760 --> 00:14:28.100
[COBRA coughing]

259
00:14:23.520 --> 00:14:24.320
Lili...

260
00:14:28.770 --> 00:14:31.230
[COBRA] No one is meant
to sit upon that throne.

261
00:14:32.920 --> 00:14:35.740
[COBRA] The world should
not bend to one person's will!

262
00:14:35.820 --> 00:14:37.530
This was the oath!

263
00:14:37.610 --> 00:14:40.340
[IMU] There are two things
that I wish to tell you,

264
00:14:40.770 --> 00:14:44.280
and one thing I wish
to ask of you, Cobra.

265
00:14:44.630 --> 00:14:46.290
But who are you?

266
00:14:48.160 --> 00:14:50.180
The name Imu sounds familiar.

267
00:14:50.800 --> 00:14:52.610
Surely it's a coincidence,

268
00:14:52.490 --> 00:14:58.620
[IMU] Cease your prying.
I will not respond to it.

269
00:14:53.000 --> 00:14:55.080
But among the First
Twenty there was...

270
00:15:00.260 --> 00:15:03.130
But I shall answer
your previous question.

271
00:15:04.070 --> 00:15:06.610
The "D." you speak
of is the name of those

272
00:15:06.610 --> 00:15:09.340
who once opposed
us long ago.

273
00:15:09.340 --> 00:15:10.840
[gasps]

274
00:15:10.840 --> 00:15:12.260
[IMU] It has reared
its ugly head

275
00:15:12.260 --> 00:15:14.850
rather frequently
in recent years

276
00:15:14.850 --> 00:15:17.230
among hollow shells who
don't even know the meaning

277
00:15:17.230 --> 00:15:19.270
of their own name.

278
00:15:19.270 --> 00:15:22.910
That wretched faction,
like so many other scourges,

279
00:15:22.910 --> 00:15:27.880
stemmed from Queen Lili's
great mistake 800 years ago.

280
00:15:28.160 --> 00:15:29.280
What mistake?

281
00:15:29.560 --> 00:15:31.600
[IMU] We have her to thank
for those scholars

282
00:15:31.740 --> 00:15:35.290
who were sniffing around
the Void Century as well.

283
00:15:35.290 --> 00:15:38.000
And for the pirates,
who seek the Poneglyphs

284
00:15:38.000 --> 00:15:41.000
in their never-ending
search for treasure.

285
00:15:41.000 --> 00:15:44.460
Were it not for Lili's
mistake on that fateful day,

286
00:15:44.460 --> 00:15:48.210
those stones would never have
been scattered across the world,

287
00:15:48.820 --> 00:15:52.480
and not a soul would covet
the loathsome things.

288
00:15:57.700 --> 00:16:00.390
[IMU] A damning
question must be asked.

289
00:16:00.830 --> 00:16:03.310
Was this travesty
an accident?

290
00:16:03.630 --> 00:16:05.880
Were the Poneglyphs
truly unleashed

291
00:16:05.950 --> 00:16:09.960
upon the world by mistake?

292
00:16:10.270 --> 00:16:13.410
Or was it all by design?

293
00:16:13.860 --> 00:16:15.570
[gasps]

294
00:16:20.260 --> 00:16:22.300
[IMU] I believe you
know the answer.

295
00:16:22.340 --> 00:16:24.360
It must have been
written in Lili's letter

296
00:16:24.360 --> 00:16:28.210
that arrived in Alabasta.

297
00:16:28.210 --> 00:16:31.300
I cannot help but notice that
you have referred to her only

298
00:16:31.300 --> 00:16:34.720
as "Queen Lili
of the Nefertari Family."

299
00:16:35.420 --> 00:16:37.200
Why is that?

300
00:16:37.940 --> 00:16:43.400
What is the proper name
written on that letter. Say it.

301
00:16:51.150 --> 00:16:52.250
[COBRA] That settles it.

302
00:16:52.760 --> 00:16:55.060
My hopes were
already dwindling,

303
00:16:55.140 --> 00:16:58.380
but now I'm certain I won't
be leaving this room alive.

304
00:17:01.380 --> 00:17:04.440
If I renounce the truth,
then would you let me go?

305
00:17:04.510 --> 00:17:05.510
Your fate was sealed

306
00:17:05.510 --> 00:17:07.500
the moment you laid
eyes on Great Imu.

307
00:17:07.980 --> 00:17:10.070
A lie will change nothing.

308
00:17:24.320 --> 00:17:25.460
[COBRA] Of course it won't.

309
00:17:26.010 --> 00:17:28.830
I've uncovered the greatest
secret in the world.

310
00:17:35.150 --> 00:17:36.620
[SABO] What's
going on in there?

311
00:17:37.080 --> 00:17:38.640
Something is very wrong.

312
00:17:40.280 --> 00:17:42.100
The letter that you speak of

313
00:17:42.490 --> 00:17:46.700
was signed by the queen
of Alabasta 800 years ago.

314
00:17:47.100 --> 00:17:48.860
Her full name was...

315
00:17:52.500 --> 00:17:54.920
...Nefertari...

316
00:17:57.960 --> 00:18:01.130
...D. Lili.

317
00:18:01.230 --> 00:18:03.230
[IMU] "D."

318
00:18:18.500 --> 00:18:19.460
[gasps]

319
00:18:20.040 --> 00:18:20.870
[SABO] Fire Fist!

320
00:18:26.280 --> 00:18:27.110
Rook Check!

321
00:18:32.110 --> 00:18:33.990
[IMU] Where did
you come from?

322
00:18:47.180 --> 00:18:48.560
[gasps]

323
00:19:02.740 --> 00:19:06.010
Seems it was naive of me
to think I could take you down.

324
00:19:06.010 --> 00:19:09.950
I didn't expect to find hell up
here at the top of the world.

325
00:19:25.810 --> 00:19:27.070
You stay away!

326
00:19:28.620 --> 00:19:31.760
[COBRA coughs]

327
00:19:31.760 --> 00:19:37.430
Young man. You're him,
aren't you? Luffy's brother.

328
00:19:40.720 --> 00:19:46.220
You're a Revolutionary.
Why would you protect a king?

329
00:19:46.540 --> 00:19:49.560
Our true enemies are the ones
who sit above the kings.

330
00:19:49.640 --> 00:19:50.850
These monsters.

331
00:19:51.360 --> 00:19:53.350
But wait, how do
you know Luffy?

332
00:19:54.890 --> 00:19:56.930
Well, he saved my life.

333
00:19:57.990 --> 00:19:59.070
[chuckles] Sounds like him.

334
00:20:07.430 --> 00:20:09.350
I know it hurts, but hold on.

335
00:20:09.350 --> 00:20:11.820
I'm gonna do my best
to get you ou...

336
00:20:21.420 --> 00:20:23.890
You won't escape with me
slowing you down.

337
00:20:24.010 --> 00:20:27.430
I'm going to die either way.
Please, just leave me.

338
00:20:27.820 --> 00:20:28.670
Not a chance!

339
00:20:30.740 --> 00:20:33.020
I discovered
something important.

340
00:20:34.740 --> 00:20:37.510
No matter what, I need
you to leave here alive.

341
00:20:37.920 --> 00:20:41.520
You have to pass on a message
to Luffy and Vivi for me.

342
00:20:41.600 --> 00:20:43.370
If you say so, but what is it?

343
00:20:44.610 --> 00:20:47.650
Tell them that we all
share the name "D."

344
00:20:47.650 --> 00:20:48.990
[gasps]

345
00:20:54.040 --> 00:20:56.200
[SABO] It can't be
a coincidence, right?

346
00:20:56.720 --> 00:20:58.610
What do you mean?
What can't?

347
00:20:58.640 --> 00:21:00.150
You both have the same...

348
00:21:00.150 --> 00:21:02.020
[LUFFY] They're done!
They're done!

349
00:21:02.020 --> 00:21:04.270
Ha! Looks tasty!

350
00:21:04.400 --> 00:21:06.420
Hey! You can't
eat two at once!

351
00:21:06.420 --> 00:21:07.900
Yeah I can! I'm hungry!

352
00:21:07.900 --> 00:21:10.060
He means they won't
fit in your face!

353
00:21:10.530 --> 00:21:12.030
Mmm, yummy!

354
00:21:12.460 --> 00:21:13.610
Well, okay, then.

355
00:21:17.920 --> 00:21:19.580
Wow. It's great.

356
00:21:20.080 --> 00:21:22.890
Anyway, what were you
about to say, Sabo?

357
00:21:22.970 --> 00:21:25.580
Oh. I was just about to ask.

358
00:21:25.610 --> 00:21:27.050
How come both
of you guys' names

359
00:21:27.050 --> 00:21:28.980
have the letter
"D." in the middle?

360
00:21:29.300 --> 00:21:30.150
[LUFFY] D?

361
00:21:30.560 --> 00:21:33.930
[SABO] Monkey D.
Luffy and Portgas D. Ace.

362
00:21:34.220 --> 00:21:35.880
There's a "D." in both.

363
00:21:36.400 --> 00:21:37.780
Oh, yeah, I guess so!

364
00:21:38.310 --> 00:21:40.900
I don't know why,
but who cares about names?

365
00:21:41.540 --> 00:21:43.090
You want a "D.," too, Sabo?

366
00:21:43.550 --> 00:21:44.460
Huh?

367
00:21:44.460 --> 00:21:45.380
Sa-D.-Bo!

368
00:21:45.380 --> 00:21:47.170
C'mon, don't put it there!

369
00:21:47.170 --> 00:21:50.510
Yeah, and who's gonna stop
me? Your name's Sa-D.-Bo!

370
00:21:50.510 --> 00:21:53.590
[LUFFY, ACE laugh]

371
00:21:53.780 --> 00:21:58.660
[laughs]

372
00:21:59.230 --> 00:21:59.700
Finally.

373
00:22:00.960 --> 00:22:05.790
Finally, I see the path forward
that Alabasta must take.

374
00:22:05.790 --> 00:22:07.290
Don't die! Just hang on!

375
00:22:07.330 --> 00:22:09.590
We're gonna get you
through this, okay?

376
00:22:11.880 --> 00:22:13.050
[gasps]

377
00:22:13.050 --> 00:22:14.340
[SABO yelps]

378
00:22:21.900 --> 00:22:22.990
[SABO] King Cobra!

379
00:22:37.150 --> 00:22:38.120
King Cobra!

380
00:22:40.220 --> 00:22:41.470
"The Poneglyphs"...

381
00:22:45.790 --> 00:22:49.500
"Bear the flag
of a new dawn"...

382
00:22:50.340 --> 00:22:54.760
"Nefertari D. Lili"...

383
00:22:55.090 --> 00:22:56.750
I'm counting on you.

384
00:23:05.420 --> 00:23:07.240
[COBRA] I'm counting
on you, Sabo.

385
00:23:11.160 --> 00:23:12.130
King Cobra!

386
00:23:17.190 --> 00:23:18.740
[COBRA] You must live on!
